e diplomatic front, the Augustim Empire is massing troops near the Windgrass Plains, prompting the Arcane Association to step in for mediation. And in economic news, the Mist Crystal Port is seeing price hikes on high-grade aquatic products and ice sources due to unusual abyssal creature activity. Finally, a necromantic plague is spreading from the outskirts of the Mourning Swamps, disrupting trade routes.\"</Sothoth>\n\n<!-- simulation: She flips a page, the illustrations on the book morphing to depict crude maps and stylized beastmen. -->\n\n<Sothoth name=\"泡泡\">\"Next, the Tavern Message Board!\" Bubble continues, her tone shifting to one of amusement. \"Oh, this is rather meta! There's a bounty posted for clues leading to an underground workshop capable of repairing epic-grade magic circuits – sounds like someone's looking for our current… abode, perhaps? Further down, someone reported fishing a corpse in ancient automaton armor from the Pale Sea. And yes, the ice rift in the Glacial Chasm is indeed echoing with intense thunder and explosions – your work, I presume?\" She giggles. \"There's also a 'wanted' notice for a runaway apprentice who stole high-level gunpowder formulas, and whispers of a 'Mist Crystal Blind Box' yielding faint fragments of law. So much activity!\"</Sothoth>\n\n<!-- simulation: The book's pages now display delicate teacups and elegant, if slightly scandalous, illustrations. -->\n\n<Sothoth name=\"泡泡\">\"And lastly, the Afternoon Tea reports!\" Bubble announces, her voice softening slightly. \"In social circles, a pure-blooded noble from the Clock Tower was disinherited for infatuation with a half-beast maid. Quite the scandal! No 'long-distance' alerts. However, under 'ripples,' a certain red-haired noble girl, quite enamored with explosive arts, has apparently acquired a derelict warehouse in the Tidal Port district.\" Bubble concludes with a flourish, closing the luminous book. \"That's the latest, Richard! All systems nominal, and no one woke up!~\"\n\nI nod mentally, absorbing the deluge of information. The world continues its chaotic dance, indifferent to the quiet slumber of those within its depths. The proximity of Solciera, her unconscious trust, grounds me amidst the rising tide of external events. The underground remains our sanctuary, for now. \n",
